.TH OTSDAQ-MU2E-CALORIMETER-ROOT-MACROS 7 "2026-10-06" "otsdaq-mu2e-calorimeter 9.01.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
otsdaq-mu2e-calorimeter-root-macros \- index of the ROOT macros in otsdaq-mu2e-calorimeter/scripts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B root \-l \-b \-q
.RI ' macro .C+( arguments )'
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.I scripts/
directory of otsdaq-mu2e-calorimeter holds six ROOT macros for expert
use.
They are not built or installed by CMake, have no command-line
interface of their own, and are run through ROOT's interpreter or ACLiC.
The entry point of each macro is the function with the file's base name,
except where noted.
.PP
The DTC macros include headers by a path relative to a development
area, for example
.IR srcs/mu2e_pcie_utils/dtcInterfaceLib/DTC.h ,
so they must be started from the top of a Spack or mrb development
area in which
.I srcs/
holds the sources.
.SS Macros
.TP
.BI calo_gr4_generate_txt( inputFileName ", " outputName ", " option )
Reads the TTree
.I pulseIERCAnalysis/tree
written by the
.B CaloiercAnalyzer
art module and writes the per-channel timing data it contains to the text
file
.IR outputName .
.TP
.BI converter( run_num )
Reads the binary file
.IR macroOutput_ run_num .bin
from the current directory and writes its header and payload words as
hexadecimal text to
.IR $OTSDAQ_DATA/header_ run_num .txt
and
.IR $OTSDAQ_DATA/payload_ run_num .txt .
The progress message names
.I $OTSDAQ_DATA
as the input directory, but the input is opened relative to the current
directory.
.TP
.BI dtc_validate( NEvents )
A stub: it only prints
.RB \(lq Ciao \(rq.
.TP
.BI validate_pattern( ievtno ", " file_name )
Reads
.IR file_name .bin ,
checks a variable-size, +1-counter test pattern from the calorimeter and
tracker ROCs, and writes mismatches to
.RI error_ file_name .txt .
The number of links is set by editing
.B LINK_NO
and
.B FIRST_LINK
in the source.
.TP
.BI write_dcs_roc_block( Link ", " ROCSleepTime )
Builds a DCS block-write payload of 16-bit words (floats split into two
words) for a ROC on DTC link
.IR Link .
The part that opens the DTC and performs the write is commented out, so
the macro currently only builds and prints the payload.
.TP
.BI write_testfranco( Link ", " ROCSleepTime )
In
.IR write_test.C ;
opens the DTC in
.B DTC_SimMode_NoCFO
mode with only
.I Link
enabled and runs a ROC register and block write test.
.I write_test.C
also defines
.BR write_roc_1() .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I scripts/*.C
The macros.
.TP
.IR scripts/converter_C.so ", " scripts/converter_C.d ", " scripts/converter_C_ACLiC_dict_rdict.pcm ", " scripts/dtc_validate_C.d
ACLiC build products that are tracked in git.
They were built against ROOT v6_28_04c from
.I /cvmfs/mu2e.opensciencegrid.org/artexternals
and are stale; delete them and let ACLiC rebuild.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OTSDAQ_DATA
Output directory of
.BR converter() .
.SH EXAMPLES
Convert run 105 from a development area that contains
.IR macroOutput_105.bin :
.PP
.RS
.nf
export OTSDAQ_DATA=$PWD/data
root \-l \-b \-q 'srcs/otsdaq_mu2e_calorimeter/scripts/converter.C+("105")'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Extract IERC timing data from a
.B CaloiercAnalyzer
output file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
root \-l \-b \-q \e
  'scripts/calo_gr4_generate_txt.C("ierc.root","ierc_times.txt",0)'
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR root (1),
.BR slow_control_summary.sh (1)
.PP
.I doc/INTERFACES.md
in the otsdaq-mu2e-calorimeter source tree.
.SH AUTHOR
Macros by the Mu2e calorimeter and DAQ groups.
Index page written for the September 2026 Mu2e DAQ review.
